    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • The Volkswagen Group's Affordable BEV Quartet Has Almost Reached 150,000 Orders\nElectrified-Only 2027 Lexus NX SUV Lands with Multiple Upgrades and a Touch of Mars\n96 photos\nPhoto: Lexus\nAfter at the end of last week Japanese luxury carmaker Lexus stepped into the spotlight with the 2027 model year interpretation of the TX SUV, it now does the same for the NX crossover. This time, however, the list of changes imagined for this vehicle is far richer.\nPerhaps the most important thing to note about the NX is that from now on there will be no version of it that’s powered exclusively by an internal combustion engine. For 2027, the NX will come to market only as a hybrid and a plug-in hybrid.\nThe upgrades the carmaker imagined for the refreshed range target, thus, a powertrain realignment, exterior and interior nips and tucks, and a little touch of extra features. Why, for one reason or another, there’s also a connection to planet Mars to discuss.\nThe overall look of the SUV remains the same as before, but refined in key places in a way that also includes functional elements that target aerodynamics and cooling performance. Finer touches, including a switch from chrome to black for the mirrors and moldings, are also included in the package, as is the first-time use of the double L signature for the rear lamps.\nThe 2027 NX will be offered on the American market in nine exterior colors, including three new ones: Shaded Ivy, Incognito, and Iridium, which, on top of being a new addition, also replaces the previous Atomic Silver.\nPhoto: Lexus The cabin of the NX has suffered changes as well, with the most noticeable being the revised steering wheel, which now displays the brand’s name in the new font the company went for this year. On top of that, it’s smaller than it used to be, dropping by 0.4 inches to 14.2 inches.\nThe dashboard is dominated by the two horizontally aligned screens, the 12.3-inch instrument display and the 14-inch infotainment system. The latter is now offered as standard across all the trim levels.\nLexus throws on the table five interior colors for the NX, two of which, Abalos and Radiant Red, are new. It is here that the connection with planet Mars comes in, as Abalos is, apparently, inspired by the sand dunes that exist in the northern hemisphere of the Red Planet.\nAs said, there will be only hybrid and plug-in hybrid variants of the NX available for the 2027 model year. When it comes to the former, the chosen name is NX 350h, and the selected powertrain is a combination of a 2.5-liter gasoline engine, a front motor generator, and a rear axle motor. Combined, these bits of hardware are rated at 244 hp, four hp more than in the previous version.\nPhoto: Lexus The same 2.5-liter gasoline engine is at the core of the plug-in hybrid NX 450h+ as well, only this time it works with a newly developed lithium-ion battery that’s good for up to 45 miles (72 km) of pure electric driving.\nThe SUV now has an upgraded front electric motor, whose power levels grew from 180 hp to 203 hp, with the one at the rear throwing in an extra 54 hp. The total, combined power of the plug-in hybrid NX stands at 324 hp, 20 more than before.\nTechnically speaking, the powertrain setup for both versions is not unheard of, but Lexus does speak about having deployed the most advanced hybrid drivetrain technology in the NX, paired with the revised version of the ICE unit.\nWe’re told about a redesigned engine block casting with reinforced areas for improved block rigidity and reduced noise and vibration. On its own, no matter the application, the engine delivers 186 horsepower at 6,000 rpm and 173 lb-ft of torque at 4,200 rpm.\nPhoto: Lexus Both versions of the NX are equipped with an e-Axle assembly that brings together in the same package the transaxle, motor, and power control unit. An all-wheel-drive system comes as standard on certain trim levels.\nSpeaking of configurations, there are three of them for the NX 350h (FWD, AWD, and F Sport), and two for the NX 450h+ (standard and F Sport). The top-of-the-range F Sport brings along, for both powertrains, several unique features, including under spoilers, side pontoons, and rear corner rocker panels, among other things.\nThese drivetrain setups can be had in combination with no less than six trim levels for the hybrid and four for the plug-in hybrid . For now, Lexus has not released any information on what each of them brings to market.\nLexus did not specifically say when the 2027 NX will become available to order, but it probably won’t be long now. We’ll keep an eye on the Japanese carmaker and report back as soon as it announces how much the refreshed crossover will cost.\nJust like before, the new hybrid Lexus NX will be assembled at the Toyota Motor Manufacturing Canada (TMMC) facility in Ontario, Canada, while the plug-in hybrid comes from the Toyota Motor Kyushu (TMK) plant in Japan.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nLexus Lexus NX SUV\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Daniel Patrascu\nDaniel loves writing (or so he claims), and he uses this skill to offer readers a \"behind the scenes\" look at the automotive industry. He also enjoys talking about space exploration and robots, because in his view the only way forward for humanity is away from this planet, in metal bodies. Full profile\nUP NEXT 1968 Mustang GT 390 Time Capsule Surfaces With Rarest Factory Option, Original Owner Had It 57 Years",
